# Copy to dev/.env on zero. .env is gitignored — it holds absolute host paths, and the
# *_SECRETS directories hold live key material.
#
# Absolute paths, never $HOME: HOME is unset or root's under sudo and cron, and the
# Makefile runs docker through sudo. That rule is one of this repo's three, in ../README.md.
#
# EVERY LINE BELOW IS REQUIRED, even for a container whose profile is off: Compose
# refuses a required variable it cannot fill even in a service whose profile is off
# (compose.yaml's header). The paths for the other repos are their existing clones on zero.

# ── which containers ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The services `make up` starts beyond the hub and infra-dev: `tunnel` once the hub's tunnel
# is provisioned (below), and each other container that should be up at rest. dd-dev and
# ds-dev have been stopped at rest; `make up S=dd-dev` starts one when wanted.
COMPOSE_PROFILES=tunnel,or3-dev

# The containers the hub's menu and offloader reach, by name, in menu order. A stopped one
# reads "not answering" in the menu and costs nothing. Space-separated.
HUB_HOSTS=infra-dev or3-dev dd-dev ds-dev

# ── the hub ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Mode-700 directory OUTSIDE the repo, written by
#     ansible-playbook playbooks/server-create-dev-container.yml -e container=dev
# holding:
#   authorized_keys   the clients allowed to ssh to `dev` — the phone, the PCs
#   tunnel.json       the hub tunnel's credentials, gavin-owned 0600 (the sidecar runs as gavin)
HUB_SECRETS=/home/gavin/.dev-secrets
# The TunnelID in $HUB_SECRETS/tunnel.json — cloudflared's `tunnel run` needs it on its
# command line, and the image has no shell to read it out of the file. Printed by that play.
HUB_TUNNEL_ID=
# 0 stops the hub's offload timer: no container's idle sessions are stopped.
HUB_OFFLOAD=1
# THE GITHUB TOKEN BROKER, off while empty (dev/README.md § "GitHub tokens, one repo each").
# The id of the GitHub App you made for the hub; its private key goes in $HUB_SECRETS as
# github-app.pem, 0600. Each container then gets an hourly token for its own repo only.
HUB_GITHUB_APP_ID=
# What every token may do, never more than the App was granted. Unset is the default in
# compose.yaml: contents, pull requests, issues and workflows to write; actions, checks and
# statuses to read.
# HUB_GITHUB_PERMISSIONS=contents=write,pull_requests=write

# ── the pool ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Empty until hosts/zero/system/'s pool file is installed and proved (plans/dev-pool.md,
# step 1); then /devpool, and `make up`.
DEV_CGROUP_PARENT=

# ── infra-dev ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Mode-700 directory OUTSIDE the repo, written by the dev-container playbook:
#   authorized_keys            public keys allowed to ssh straight in (break glass)
#   id_ed25519_infra_deploy    GitHub deploy key for gsfernandes81/infra (generated on zero)
#   id_ed25519_fleet           the key that reaches zero, one and two — absent by decision
#   ssh_config.fleet / known_hosts.fleet   the same, absent by decision
# Mounted read-only; the entrypoint copies out of it and never writes back.
INFRA_SECRETS=/home/gavin/.infra-dev-secrets
# A cap, not a reservation; dev/README.md has why it is lower than or3-dev's.
DEV_MEM_LIMIT=1024m
DEV_MEMSWAP_LIMIT=1536m
# 0 makes the hub's offload passes stop nothing in any dev container.
DEV_IDLE_OFFLOAD=1
GIT_USER_NAME=Gavin Fernandes
GIT_USER_EMAIL=gavinfernandes2012@pm.me

# ── the other repos' containers ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Each SECRETS is that container's mode-700 keys directory, mounted read-only: or3's is written
# by its dev/seed-secrets.sh and also lends its deploy key to the image build (or3 is private);
# dd's and ds's are what was each clone's .dev-ssh/, moved out at the cutover. No repo's clone
# on zero is read by anything: each child builds from GitHub (compose.yaml).
OR3_SECRETS=/home/gavin/.or3-dev-secrets
DD_SECRETS=/home/gavin/.dd-dev-secrets
DS_SECRETS=/home/gavin/.ds-dev-secrets
